BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Video Editing with Da Vinci Resolve Parts I and II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270108T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270115T160000
UID:6b09a0dfbe13a7003363951a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This two part introductory series will cover the layout\, t
 ools and workflow used for video editing in DaVinci Resolve. Part I\, whi
 ch will take place on\nJanuary 8th\n\, will cover basic video editing tec
 hniques such as inserting and trimming media\, transitions\, titles\, addi
 ng audio\, and using flags and markers.\nPart II will be held on\nJanuary 
 15th\n\, where participants will become familiar with some of the more adv
 anced tools in DaVinci’s Editing page such as key framing transform effe
 cts\, cropping\, adjusting clip speed\, normalizing audio\, and simple com
 positing.\nComputers will be provided for this program.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Spadina Road
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b09a0dfbe13a7003363951a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Origami Lotus Flowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T180000
UID:6aac152519094f0c6938b75a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a six-part workshop series that creates a space for ex
 ploring belonging and not belonging through conversation and hands-on art-
 making. Guided by reflective questions\, participants engage in practices 
 such as origami with washi\, drawing\, dyeing\, and writing\, using the lo
 tus as a shared symbol of transformation and resilience across cultures. T
 he workshops foster an inclusive\, supportive environment\, particularly f
 or those who feel marginalized or disconnected. The series culminates in a
  collaborative public floral installation in the library\, sharing partici
 pants’ work with the wider community.\nLed by artists "Being~inbetween"\
 nThe workshops are open to youth\, ages 13-17\, and require no prior artis
 tic experience.\nWorkshop Dates:\nFriday\, September 11th\nFriday\, Septem
 ber 18th\nFriday\, October 30th\nFriday\, November 6th\nFriday\, December 
 4th\nFriday\, December 11th
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac152519094f0c6938b75a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
