BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Boba Drink Making Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270122T154500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270122T163000
UID:6b00c0f6c58b38184c083b96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Chef Yumiko leads a hands-on workshop to make the popular Asia
 n beverage\, Brown Sugar Milk with Boba.  Participants will learn to prepa
 re and use the classic ingredients​ including milk\, molasses and tapioc
 a pearls to make this visually pleasing and sweet drink. Chef Yumiko will 
 also provide a brief history of Boba and why it's so popular globally.\n(*
 contains dairy\, sugar\, and caffeine)\nSnacks and refreshments are provid
 ed for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the progra
 m. Please disclose any food allergies upon registration.\nThis program is 
 part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens afte
 r school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Fr
 ee\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth 
 Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\
 nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public 
 Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d
 ). The information will only be used for event and program registration\, 
 delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b00c0f6c58b38184c083b96
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
