BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Affirmations to Confidence with Joshua Watkis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T170000
UID:6b05ad468f67a82b03123265@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, Coach Joshua Watkis will address the self-s
 crutiny faced by youth in the digital age by using poetry and self-reflect
 ion as tools for positive  reinforcement. Participants will learn how to 
 identify\, affirm\, and articulate their intrinsic value by mastering the 
 basics of metaphors and similes and utilizing the psychological and poetic
  power of targeted repetition and group affirmations.\nThis program is for
  teens (ages 13-17). Registration required.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Earlscourt room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b05ad468f67a82b03123265
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
